  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Screen and keys",
      "items": [
        "Four key rows sit above row 1: s summary and 0 quick paste in dark amber, a audio only and v video only in the brighter amber, then the 14 numbered rows.",
        "Two blue notice lines sit under the box rule: the four direct keys on the first, the clipboard clause on the second, at 52 columns each inside the 64-column width.",
        "The keys fire only on the main prompt's empty line, so a pasted url is never read as a key.",
        "Escape backs out of a submenu, wipes results, and stops a running download with rc 130 after cleaning partials."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "List input (FR-24)",
      "items": [
        "split_urls cuts a paste on commas, newlines and a standalone 0 token; a 0 inside a url stays part of it, because video ids carry zeros.",
        "The four direct keys run every url in paste order, print 'url i of n' when there is more than one, and stop the rest on rc 130.",
        "Item 1 asks the mode first - enter or 0 full, a audio, v video, s summary - and repeats an unknown answer.",
        "Its list takes one url per line or a whole paste; a line with no link stays in the list as a marked error row."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Offered-track walk (FR-9)",
      "items": [
        "A pass that wrote no subtitle file probes the offer once: language, native tracks and automatic tracks, keys only, under 1 KB per video.",
        "Candidates run from the native track in the video language to the requested pattern; generated translations are never candidates because they answer 429.",
        "At most four tries run automatically, each printed as 'subtitle fallback - ...'; escape during a try ends the run with rc 130.",
        "do_summary runs the same walk before it gives up on text and falls back to sound.",
        "The s key strips the fresh files to text in text mode whatever the stored stripper settings say; only no text at all falls back to sound."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Release matrix (FR-25)",
      "items": [
        "Six cli-bearing bundles: windows x64 zip, windows arm64 zip, linux x64 and arm64 tars, linux x64 and arm64 musl tars; macOS ships a pkg and never self-updates.",
        "release_asset maps platform, arch and libc to the archive named for the release tag, so a bundle-matrix change moves the lookup in the same commit.",
        "The windows arm64 bundle carries the x64 ffmpeg under emulation; the arm64 binaries are built on native arm64 runners.",
        "The updater reads tag, asset and digest in one GET, gates the digest, runs the quiet selftest, and renames the image into place."
      ]
    }
  ]
